# Temporal Workflows - Complete Implementation Guide

**CRITICAL: ALL implementations MUST include Runtime Kill Switch**

## Runtime Kill Switch (MANDATORY)

**Environment Variable:** `TEMPORAL_STATE` (set in module's `.env` file)  
**Values:** `ON` | `OFF`  
**Default:** `ON` (if not set)

**Every service/controller calling Temporal workflows MUST check this variable FIRST:**

```java
// Java Example - Controller with Kill Switch
@RestController
public class OrderController {
    @Autowired
    private OrderService orderService;
    
    @Autowired
    private OrderWorkflowClient temporalClient;
    
    @Autowired
    private Environment env;
    
    @PostMapping("/api/orders")
    public ResponseEntity<OrderResult> createOrder(@RequestBody OrderRequest request) {
        // ✅ MANDATORY: Check kill switch FIRST
        String temporalState = env.getProperty("TEMPORAL_STATE", "ON").toUpperCase();
        
        if ("OFF".equals(temporalState)) {
            // Temporal DISABLED - bypass, execute directly
            logger.warn("Temporal bypassed - TEMPORAL_STATE=OFF in .env");
            return ResponseEntity.ok(orderService.processOrderDirect(request));
        } else {
            // Temporal ENABLED - execute via workflow
            return ResponseEntity.ok(temporalClient.executeOrderWorkflow(request));
        }
    }
}
```

